    "@value" : "A fee representing the gap between tuition fees and other funding"
  }, {
    "@value" : "A tuition fee for a course includes the maximum amount covered by a VET Student Loan and the remaining tuition cost not covered by the loan – the ‘gap fee’. As it’s part of the tuition fee, the gap fee can’t include fees for non-tuition services such as items and equipment that become the student’s physical property and are not consumed in the course (for example, maps, charts or textbooks)."
  } ],
