  "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#definition" : [ {
    "@value" : "Costs include any co-investment or additional training and assessment costs above the funding band, that the employer has paid directly to the provider, where this is part of the agreed apprenticeship."
  }, {
    "@value" : "Main providers and employer-providers receiving funding for delivering apprenticeship training and on-programme assessment in England"
  }, {
    "@value" : "Mentoring must meet the definition of off-the-job training (new learning, relevant to the apprenticeship, not English and maths, delivered within normal working hours) and be documented in the training plan. The mentor must be a more senior or experienced member of staff. This does not include general line management. The apprentice must not be doing productive work."
  }, {
    "@value" : "The full range of fees retained by the provider and charges (which must be eligible costs) that apply, including funding retained for managing quality assurance / oversight and for administrative functions such as data returns."
  }, {
    "@value" : "These rules form part of the terms and conditions for the use of funds in an employer’s apprenticeship service account or for government-employer co-investment."
  } ],
